From f9f601d62275c4631bba7ae5a3747652cd1f2984 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 09:45:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Shiro: unpckhpd's low half is the destination's high half (it
 took the source's)

llvmpipe's shader code (Mesa, LLVM 15) uses unpckhpd to move high halves;
Blink copied the source's high quadword into both halves, so 3 of 5 sampled
pixels of a GLSL test shader were wrong (unix/gui's osmesa-probe). Test:
fixtures/x86/sse41b.c, LLVM's SSE4.1 forms with REX registers and memory
operands, against native.
---
 blink/ssefloat.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/blink/ssefloat.c b/blink/ssefloat.c
index 09591ea..115f159 100644
--- a/blink/ssefloat.c
+++ b/blink/ssefloat.c
@@ -107,7 +107,7 @@ void OpUnpckhpsd(P) {
   b = GetModrmRegisterXmmPointerRead16(A);
   IGNORE_RACES_START();
   if (Osz(rde)) {
-    memcpy(a + 0, b + 8, 8);
+    memcpy(a + 0, a + 8, 8);  // unpckhpd: the destination's high half, then the source's
     memcpy(a + 8, b + 8, 8);
   } else {
     memcpy(a + 4 * 0, a + 4 * 2, 4);
-- 
